// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Tool marks for the /about skills chapter.
//
// Inlined rather than added as a dependency, for the same reason the glyphs
// in ./index.tsx are: this needs seventeen marks, and simple-icons ships
// 3,453. The path data is copied verbatim from two sets and regenerated by
// hand if a mark ever changes.
//
//   simple-icons 16.28.0  CC0-1.0        24x24, one path, built for currentColor
//   devicon                MIT            128x128, `-plain` variant, fill stripped
//
// Trademarks belong to their owners; these identify tools that are used.
//
// NOT HERE, and why: neither set carries Excel, Power BI, Codex, SQL,
// Antigravity or Visual Paradigm. The Microsoft and Adobe marks were
// withdrawn from simple-icons at the brands' request, so they were not worth
// sourcing from somewhere less careful. Those six are supplied by hand
// instead and drawn as masks; see the `logo` field in content/skills.ts.
//
// "Hermes Agent" is supplied for a different reason: simple-icons' `hermes`
// is the parcel carrier, not Nous Research.
//
// A chip with no mark at all is still not a broken chip. It renders as the
// page's ordinary .tag, which is what it is.
//
// To add one: drop `{ vb, d }` in below and reference the key from
// content/skills.ts.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

